      "title": "Exact centered squared-defect coercivity and bounded inverse",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A2",
          "label": "PBPS2609.06905v1 AppendixB B1-B5, D1-D2 real L2 stationarity/centering, C4/B15 squared-defect precursor; exact31regions/54items source inventory independently covered.",
          "scope": "SAME actual55 T on L2(nu), selfadjoint/mean preserving/constant fixed, exact complete mean-zero restriction T0, full and centered positive squared defects; real Test uses actual58 rho/delta to prove IsUnit centered squared defect. No Gamma/root/polar/full weakH1/hypocoercivity/dynamics/main/implementation error/cost/composition/fullpaper/Goal admission."
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        "lake build Tests.ProximalBPSCenteredDefect"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "The complete potential, curvature, initialization law and step conditions are stated above. No operator, probability, stationarity, mean-zero preservation or coercivity certificate is supplied by the caller.",
        "L² consists of AE classes; finite dimension of E does not make L² finite dimensional. The whole closed mean-zero subspace is used.",
        "Zero-dimensional E is explicitly included as an extension of the source Euclidean convention; αη=1 is retained."
      ],
      "statement": "E is a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume; rank zero is an explicit extension of the source Euclidean convention. V:E→ℝ is C²; 0<α≤β; α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v; η>0 and βη≤1. μ=volume.tilted(−V), J=Law(X,X+√ηZ) for independent X∼μ and Z∼N(0,I), and ν=J.snd. Finite dimensionality of E does not imply finite dimensionality of L²(ν). There exist a selfadjoint bounded operator T on L²(ν) with the literal ν-a.e. action Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx), where S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)); a class q=1 ν-a.e. with ⟨q,u⟩=∫u dν for all u; and the actual selfadjoint restriction T₀ to H₀=ker⟨q,·⟩. Set ρ=(1−αη)/(1+αη) and δ=4αη/(1+αη)². The squared defect D₀=I_H₀−T₀² is positive. For every u∈H₀, T₀u=Tu as an ambient class, ‖T₀u‖≤ρ‖u‖, ⟨D₀u,u⟩=‖u‖²−‖T₀u‖² and δ‖u‖²≤⟨D₀u,u⟩. D₀ is a unit in the algebra of bounded continuous linear endomorphisms of H₀; hence it has a bounded inverse on this exact centered space. The original hypotheses force δ>0 and include αη=1. No full-space inverse or positive square root is claimed.",
      "formula": "\\rho=\\frac{1-\\alpha\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta},\\quad\\delta=\\frac{4\\alpha\\eta}{(1+\\alpha\\eta)^2}>0,\\quad\\|T_0u\\|\\le\\rho\\|u\\|,\\quad\\langle D_0u,u\\rangle\\ge\\delta\\|u\\|^2,\\quad D_0\\in\\operatorname{GL}(H_0).",
      "boundary": "SAME actual55 T on L2(nu), selfadjoint/mean preserving/constant fixed, exact complete mean-zero restriction T0, full and centered positive squared defects; real Test uses actual58 rho/delta to prove IsUnit centered squared defect. No Gamma/root/polar/full weakH1/hypocoercivity/dynamics/main/implementation error/cost/composition/fullpaper/Goal admission.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Use the same actual reflection and actual pullback",
          "text": "Compare the AE reflection actions to identify the operator U in the verified macroscopic contraction. For the actual M from the producer, PM=M gives macro-range membership. Its AE action Mu(x,y)=u(y) and the actual marginal ν=J.snd give mean transport directly, so centered u yields a centered macro input. No extra onto witness or copied Poincare proof is needed.",
          "formula": "PMu=Mu,\\quad\\int Mu\\,dJ=\\int u\\,d\\nu=0.",
          "lean": "hSameU; hAll; hM; integral_congr_ae; integral_map"
        },
        {
          "title": "Transport the exact sharp contraction",
          "text": "Apply the verified sharp macro contraction to Mu. The actual identity MT=PUPM and the isometry transfer the constant without changing laws or operators.",
          "formula": "\\|T_0u\\|\\le\\rho\\|u\\|,\\quad\\rho=\\frac{1-\\alpha\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\in[0,1).",
          "lean": "hSharp; hCon; M.norm_map; hT0"
        },
        {
          "title": "Derive the positive coercivity constant",
          "text": "Square the contraction and use the actual quadratic defect identity. Since 0<αη≤1, the exact scalar identity yields a strictly positive lower bound, including the endpoint αη=1.",
          "formula": "\\delta=1-\\rho^2=\\frac{4\\alpha\\eta}{(1+\\alpha\\eta)^2}>0,\\quad\\delta\\|u\\|^2\\le\\langle D_0u,u\\rangle.",
          "lean": "hδ; hρ; hDef0; hGap; field_simp; ring"
        },
        {
          "title": "Obtain a bounded inverse on the centered space",
          "text": "The centered kernel is a complete Hilbert space because it is closed in L². Apply the fixed Mathlib coercivity-to-unit theorem to D₀ with δ. IsUnit means that an inverse exists in the algebra of bounded continuous linear endomorphisms of this same centered space. In the norm hypothesis, nonnegativity of the quadratic form follows directly from the already proved δ gap.",
          "formula": "D_0=I_{H_0}-T_0^2\\in\\operatorname{GL}(H_0).",
          "lean": "ContinuousLinearMap.completeSpace_ker; isUnit_of_forall_le_norm_inner_map; hUnit"
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "E is a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume; rank zero is an explicit extension of the source Euclidean convention. V:E→ℝ is C²; 0<α≤β; α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v; η>0 and βη≤1. μ=volume.tilted(−V), J=Law(X,X+√ηZ) for independent X∼μ and Z∼N(0,I), and ν=J.snd. Finite dimensionality of E does not imply finite dimensionality of L²(ν). There exist a selfadjoint bounded operator T on L²(ν) with the literal ν-a.e. action Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx), where S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)); a class q=1 ν-a.e. with ⟨q,u⟩=∫u dν for all u; and the actual selfadjoint restriction T₀ to H₀=ker⟨q,·⟩. Set ρ=(1−αη)/(1+αη) and δ=4αη/(1+αη)². The squared defect D₀=I_H₀−T₀² is positive. For every u∈H₀, T₀u=Tu as an ambient class, ‖T₀u‖≤ρ‖u‖, ⟨D₀u,u⟩=‖u‖²−‖T₀u‖² and δ‖u‖²≤⟨D₀u,u⟩. D₀ is a unit in the algebra of bounded continuous linear endomorphisms of H₀; hence it has a bounded inverse on this exact centered space. The original hypotheses force δ>0 and include αη=1. No full-space inverse or positive square root is claimed.",
      "lean_proof": "Use the same actual reflection and actual pullback; Transport the exact sharp contraction; Derive the positive coercivity constant; Obtain a bounded inverse on the centered space",
